  <data name="TutorialStepFormat" xml:space="preserve"><value>How to play · {0} of {1}</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialTitle1" xml:space="preserve"><value>One phone, the whole crew</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialText1" xml:space="preserve"><value>A game for 2–8 people. Each round, one person is the model and another one guesses. Then the roles switch.</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialTitle2" xml:space="preserve"><value>The model sees the target</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialText2" xml:space="preserve"><value>The model looks at the phone and sees a random spot on the body. Meanwhile, the guesser covers their eyes – no peeking!</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialTitle3" xml:space="preserve"><value>The touch</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialText3" xml:space="preserve"><value>The model guides the guesser’s hand and touches the chosen spot with it – exactly how and for as long as the phone shows. The guesser’s eyes stay covered.</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialTitle4" xml:space="preserve"><value>Hand over the phone</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialText4" xml:space="preserve"><value>Time’s up. The model hands over the phone. The target is hidden, so the guesser can open their eyes now.</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialTitle5" xml:space="preserve"><value>Mark the spot</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialText5" xml:space="preserve"><value>The guesser places a pin on the 3D model where the touch was. You can rotate and zoom the model and move the pin.</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialTitle6" xml:space="preserve"><value>The score</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialText6" xml:space="preserve"><value>The app measures the distance along the body’s surface. The closer to the target, the more points. A bullseye means 100 points and confetti!</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialTitle7" xml:space="preserve"><value>Switch roles</value></data>
  <data name="TutorialText7" xml:space="preserve"><value>In the next rounds the pairs change until everyone has played with everyone. The person with the most points wins.</value></data>
